// v3.0 — changes vs v2.1 (all driven by production evidence on a live retailer):
//   * RECALIBRATED. `chromium-no-client-hints` (was 25) matched 49.5% of real
//     PURCHASE revenue — Android in-app WebViews (Facebook, Instagram, TikTok…)
//     report a Chrome/ UA but send no sec-ch-ua. WebViews are now exempt from
//     that check and the residual weight is 10. No legitimate purchase scored
//     above 25 in a 7-day sample, so 70 remains a safe blocking threshold.
//   * `implausible-ios-version` (was 50) would have flagged ~26k real users
//     whose in-app browsers (NAVER, TikTok, FB…) freeze the OS token at an old
//     value (observed: "iPhone OS 15_7_2 … Version/16.5"). In-app UAs are now
//     exempt and the weight is 25 (corroborating, not decisive).
//   * NEW `ip-override-mismatch` (60). A scraper set the client IP seen by
//     GA4 to Australian addresses (via _uip / an injected X-Forwarded-For) so
//     GA4 geolocated it abroad while the CDN saw EU IPs and let it through.
//     We now compare the GA4 client's ip_override with the edge-set header;
//     a public-IP disagreement is scored. This is what caught the incident.
//   * IP resolution trusts ONLY the configured edge header (default
//     cf-connecting-ip), then the socket address. ip_override and
//     X-Forwarded-For are never used to resolve the client IP — both are
//     client-settable (Cloudflare APPENDS to an existing XFF, so first-hop
//     reads are attacker-controlled).
//   * NEW `no-sec-fetch` (15): every modern engine (Chromium 76+, Firefox 90+,
//     Safari 16.4+) sends sec-fetch-* on measurement requests; scripted HTTP
//     clients rarely bother.
//   * NEW `screen-zero` (40): a 0x0 / 1x1 screen_resolution is near-certain
//     headless.
//   * `ios-ua-with-client-hints` 70 → 60. Still a hard contradiction today
//     (no non-WebKit iOS browser has shipped, even under the EU DMA), but it
//     now needs one corroborating signal to block, so it degrades safely if
//     that ever changes.
//   * accept-language / accept-encoding stay ungated from Chromium.

